menu "Lichen sensors"
    config LICHEN_SENSORS_IMU_PERIOD_MS
        int "BMI270 sampling period (ms)"
        default 100
        range 20 1000
        help
            How often the sensors task reads the IMU (accel 100 Hz, gyro 100 Hz output rate). Apps can change it
            at run time with lichen_sensors_set_periods().

    config LICHEN_SENSORS_ENV_PERIOD_MS
        int "BME690 and P4 temperature sampling period (ms)"
        default 1000
        range 1000 60000
        help
            One forced BME690 measurement (with the gas heater, if on) and one P4 die temperature read per period.

    config LICHEN_SENSORS_I2C_HZ
        int "I2C clock for the two sensor chips (Hz)"
        default 100000
        range 100000 400000
        help
            The keyboard chip on the same bus runs at 100 kHz; both sensors can do 400 kHz.
    config LICHEN_SENSORS_GAS_HEATER
        bool "BME690 gas heater (gas resistance readings)"
        default y
        help
            The gas reading needs the BME690's hot plate at 300 C for a moment in every measurement. That heat
            reaches the chip's own temperature and humidity sensors: with the heater on they read somewhat warm
            (and humidity somewhat low), more so with a longer heater time or a shorter period. Off: no gas
            reading, no self-heating.

    config LICHEN_SENSORS_HEATER_MS
        int "Gas heater time per measurement (ms)"
        depends on LICHEN_SENSORS_GAS_HEATER
        default 100
        range 20 500
        help
            How long the hot plate is held at 300 C in each measurement (heater duty = this / the environment
            period, 10 % by default). Shorter heats less but the gas reading may not settle (gas -- in fw sensors).
endmenu
